nk). Applied: -.\n\n| Role | Leg | Side | Weight | Qty | Avg cost | Close | Unrealised | Realised | Rationale |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| winner | ONGC | LONG | 0.5 | 279 | 223.37 | 232.17 | Rs 2,454 (+3.9%) | Rs 0 | sells crude at prices linked to Brent; a higher dollar price and a weaker rupee both raise its rupee revenue per barrel |\n| loser | HINDPETRO | SHORT (PAPER SHORT: needs F&O to execute) | 0.5 | -181 | 343.63 | 352.50 | Rs -1,605 (-2.6%) | Rs 0 | buys crude in dollars and sells petrol and diesel at pump prices that move slowly; higher crude plus a weaker rupee compresses its marketing margin until prices are allowed to catch up. HINDPETRO is on the NSE F&O list, so this short could be executed with a stock future. |\n\nCombined P&L of the thesis: Rs 849 (unrealised Rs 849, realised Rs 0). Gross exposure Rs 128,578 (cap 25% of the sleeve).\n\n### Catalyst theses\n\n| Thesis | Symbol | Status | Event | Event date | Days to event | Post-event rule | Applied |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| bajaj-finance-rbi-december | BAJFINANCE | proposed | RBI Monetary Policy Committee decision, December 2026 meeting (exact date to be confirmed from the RBI calendar; estimated 4 Dec 2026) | 2026-12-04 | in 31 | hold if close on decision day > entry price, then trail stop 5% from the highest close; otherwise sell at next open | - |\n\n### Thesis fills today\n\nNo thesis fills.\n\n### Thesis orders queued for the next open\n\n| Side | Thesis | Qty / amount | Decided | Reason |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| BUY | bajaj-finance-rbi-december | Rs 75,000 | 2026-11-19 | opening catalyst: positioned two weeks before the December RBI decision |\n\n## India F&O sleeve\n\nSeparate book: Rs 500,000, NIFTY / BANKNIFTY and listed stock futures and options. Options and futures are mark-to-model (Black-Scholes / carry), not market quotes. Decisions by the daily reviewer (ROUTINE_PROMPT.md); limits in RISK_LIMITS.md.\n\n| Metric | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Sleeve equit